; Install-script policy. `allowScripts` in the root package.json decides which
; dependencies may run install scripts. This setting turns an unreviewed one
; from a warning into a failed install, which closes two gaps a warning leaves
; open: a new dependency's postinstall cannot run before someone has read it,
; and an approval that stops matching its package (a pinned entry a version
; bump left behind) fails loudly instead of quietly reverting to unreviewed.
;
; Entries denied with `false` are skipped silently and are unaffected, as are
; runs under `--ignore-scripts` or `--dangerously-allow-all-scripts`. The image
; build is out of scope twice over: it copies only the manifests and the
; lockfile, never this file, and every install it runs passes
; `--ignore-scripts` regardless.
strict-allow-scripts=true
